# fight-probe cut: the opt-in fight tests (plage01_killer_awake_prefix) take the route only up
# to this line. The T7 shore touch above (~289.6 s) has woken BaseSoldier6 out of his
# IAController `faction` stasis and sent him to the parking wall; everything after this line is
# the walked back route, chase and stake-out fight.

# ---- back route: TouchTrigger8 (passe_par_arriere) walked up the back-route nav points ----
t=296.10 goto 1282.8 -13568.0
t=303.20 goto 770.5 -12990.7
t=309.50 goto 1282.4 -12591.3
# T8 is touched at ~310.5 s; its killer-scene chain holds the player controller ~13 s, so the
# killer approach starts after the handback. TouchTrigger7 (tueur_conducteur, r850 at
# 1093,-13854) fires earlier on the shore walk (~289.6 s) - that is the game's own chain.

# ---- the killer: the walked T7 shore touch (~289.6 s) sends the killer to the parking wall;
# he parks at ~(1771,-13026) (measured with track, scratch item30c_e3/e5/e6). The north firing
# pose and a 372 UU southern spot deal zero damage (the wall blocks; measured), so the player
# walks down the proven nav legs after the T8 handback (~13 s scene hold) and fights from
# (1771,-13200), 174 UU south of him. The killer walks while attacking, so the view is tracked
# onto it. `switch_weapon 2` re-selects the picked-up Beretta (decoded InventoryGroup 2) through
# the game's own `PlayerController.SwitchWeapon` exec: the scripted T8 scene had left `Fists`
# selected (measured: without it the fires were fist swings - weapon Fists3, bone None).
t=326.00 switch_weapon 2
# ---- the chase (measured on the merged tree, scratch item30c_e18/e19): the killer leaves his
# post at ~333 and walks the map's own nav path (FindBestPathTo chain, MoveTarget samples)
# AttackPoint47 -> PathNode48 -> PathNode47 -> PathNode51 -> PathNode10 -> PathNode44 ->
# PathNode12 -> TeleportCheat1 -> PathNode41 -> PathNode43 -> PathNode39 -> PathNode17 ->
# PathNode37 -> AttackPoint14 -> PathNode36 -> AttackPoint26, parking at (-5582,-9821) from
# ~370 s. The player follows the same walkable legs (the parking wall blocks a direct
# southbound line - the shots hit it 40 UU out, scratch item30c_e21b) and fights him at his
# stake-out: the Beretta's damage (c9mmAmmo.ProcessTraceHit 0x0039, decoded) decays with
# VSize(HitLocation - W.Location) and is zero beyond ~73 UU, so the kill happens at contact
# distance where the pawn cylinders overlap. `switch_weapon 2` re-selects the picked-up Beretta
# (decoded InventoryGroup 2): the scripted T8 scene had left `Fists` selected. The game's own
# switch is the `SwitchWeapon` exec whose state machine walks PutDown -> DownWeapon -> AnimEnd ->
# Pawn.ChangedWeapon (measured by item44's test on the same pickup); `BringUp` alone is the
# engine's own no-op shadow (Weapon.Active.BringUp decodes to `bRendered = true; return`).
t=333.00 goto 770.5 -12990.7
